# Unissued 21-source copy plan

This is an inert source-copy plan. It is not an executable intake manifest, a source release, or a native validation result. Main, its index, and all existing packets remain untouched.

## Selected source changes

The E2B predecessor has twenty source/build rows. This successor changes its build donor from 868F2300 to the independently reviewed 594A048C linkage build, then appends the single FS request fixture replacement FD337AA0. The other nineteen source rows, all source preimages, and all original source-order obligations are retained.

The selected build adds the actual shared TLS/fatal/OneByte native dependency to eight selected consumers. Its separate source packet and Root acceptance establish seven actual caller paths and one conservative consumer. This plan does not claim linker or runtime qualification.

The FS fixture proposal keeps every existing control name and assertion, all production source, and the old pump loop. It owns the actual failing pump outcome across exactly one outer callback teardown. Its independent peer and Root source acceptance are deliberately unresolved here. The initial faulty proposal and the separate checker-range negative remain archived.

