## Final packet rows

The handoff adds seven separately enumerated immutable rows for this plan, its finite adaptation, source proof, authoring/checker source, two source parts, and this README. The two compiler authority snapshots are already in the core. With these seven supplemental rows and the separate future manifest, the currently planned physical total is 331 paths: nine replacements and 322 additions.

The handoff itself stays outside the future intake. A later independent peer, Root acceptance, or revised final manifest must be added explicitly after its actual bytes and hash exist. None is predicted. This arrangement avoids a manifest or handoff self-hash cycle.

## Preserved external authority

Archived JSON and source bytes are copied without rewriting historical references. The bounded logical-donor and historical-alias maps are retained. Full repository dependency members, immutable Git bases, native phase artifacts, full source/compiler seals, and Node authority inputs remain external where they were not selected archive members. The two broader clock implementation references remain explicitly outside the selected source union. This plan does not claim that the archive is a fully self-contained copy of every referenced source tree or native validation directory.

The original63 BuildQuery acceptance is observed. Its strict runtime retry1 was negative; this plan makes no runtime-positive claim. The independent negative closure, Root acceptance, complete V38 archive and actual archive commit head, fixture peer/acceptance, exact final manifest, bound intake adapter, and Root source release remain unknown or unissued.

## Future exact-byte intake contract

The accepted strengthened adapter is an unresolved source template. Its BASIS, manifest path/hash/count, actual released head, and exact final donor list still require a distinct reviewed binding. The final manifest itself participates in every donor, canonical Windows path, prefix-spelling, Git attribute, raw-versus-path conversion, raw stage-zero blob, mode, parent/commit, and final receipt gate.

All nine replacement checkout and committed preimages, every added destination, every logical content alias, the manifest, all supplemental rows, and all source modes must be rechecked at the actual Root-released head. A changed preimage or collision requires a reviewed successor. No .raw suffix, small-file, extension, or manifest exception is permitted.

The only executed code in this packet's preparation was its own bounded data/source checker and create-only evidence author. No source candidate, adapter, constructor, target, generator, compiler, Node, reference program, or native test was executed.
